+### Transferring a user to another organization
+
+`POST /orgs/{orgID}/users/{uid}/transfer` with `{"toOrgId":"globex"}` moves a
+user (for example between group companies).
+
+- Only org admins of `{orgID}` may transfer its users. Other members of the
+  organization get 403. Callers from another organization get 404 for
+  `{orgID}`.
+- `{uid}` must belong to `{orgID}`, otherwise 404.
+- `toOrgId` must name an existing organization (400 otherwise) and must differ
+  from `{orgID}` (400).
+- The move is all or nothing. The user's memberships in projects outside the
+  new organization are removed, and tasks assigned to the user in those projects
+  are unassigned. If any of those projects is archived, the whole transfer is
+  refused with 409, because archived projects are read-only.
+- Org admin rights do not move with the user: the user is no longer an org
+  admin after the transfer.
+
